These are some programs which will allow you to run DOS in your favorite 
colours. (foreground, background, and border).

There are 3 options:

1) Patch Command.COM - uses files colour??.PAT,.INS (where ?? is the first
                       two digits of your version number)
                     - Won't work if you use ANSI.SYS

2) Use CSET.COM instead of CLS command
                     - only problem is colours will be set to black and white
                       by some applications.

3) Use Rcolour.COM as a resident colour maintainer
                     - all applications that set the screen to black and white
                       will cause the program to change it to the colours you
                       have chosen

Good Luck!!

Note: Read the .INS files or .HLP files for instructions on how to use the
      various programs.

